WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.166 --> 00:00:03.669
-Last night 10 candidates

00:00:03.669 --> 00:00:05.305
faced off in
the fifth Democratic debate.

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:06.706
From the beginning
of the debate,

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:08.574
substantive policy issues
were at the forefront,

00:00:08.574 --> 00:00:09.742
and I'm just [bleep] with you.

00:00:09.742 --> 00:00:11.177
We're gonna talk
about impeachment.

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:12.378
[ Laughter ]

00:00:12.378 --> 00:00:14.580
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:18.417
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:18.417 --> 00:00:21.220
It's been an explosive week of
testimony in Washington,

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:23.889
and if you'd like an example of
just how shocking and crazy

00:00:23.889 --> 00:00:26.225
things have been, I'd like to
direct you to C-SPAN,

00:00:26.225 --> 00:00:29.662
the network of empty chairs
and sleeping congressmen.

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:32.632
C-SPAN is normally a source of
calm and consistency,

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:34.601
but the tone was
a little different today

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:36.603
when they were taking calls
on impeachment

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:38.270
and someone from Florida
called in

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:41.307
after someone from Alabama
and said this.

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:42.408
-Howdy.

00:00:42.408 --> 00:00:44.210
I just want to apologize
first and foremost

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:46.446
for all the morons
on the calls earlier,

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:48.514
especially from Alabama
and all that.

00:00:48.514 --> 00:00:51.117
Secondly I just want to say
impeach the [bleep].

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:52.018
Have a great day.

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:53.153
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:55.822
-Thanks, Monty, in Florida.

00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:57.524
That's it for phone calls
right now.

00:00:57.524 --> 00:00:58.791
-Oh, my God.

00:00:58.791 --> 00:01:00.659
Impeachment has been so crazy,

00:01:00.659 --> 00:01:03.263
C-SPAN is turning
into "Howard Stern."

00:01:03.263 --> 00:01:04.196
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.196 --> 00:01:05.531
So that's just a little glimpse

00:01:05.531 --> 00:01:07.400
in how crazy Washington's
been this week.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.102
Now, the actual
impeachment hearings

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:10.937
have been nothing short
of jaw-dropping,

00:01:10.937 --> 00:01:12.504
with one bombshell
after another.

00:01:12.504 --> 00:01:14.740
The testimony this week
has directly tied virtually

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:17.009
every senior official
in Trump's inner circle

00:01:17.009 --> 00:01:20.012
to a corrupt quid pro quo
in which the President used

00:01:20.012 --> 00:01:22.381
hundreds of millions of dollars
in taxpayer money

00:01:22.381 --> 00:01:24.917
appropriated by Congress
to solicit a bribe

00:01:24.917 --> 00:01:27.486
from a foreign country to help
him in the 2020 election.

00:01:27.486 --> 00:01:28.755
That's it.

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:30.723
That's the major takeaway I wish
everyone would remember.

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:33.058
In fact, if I knew
how to cross-stitch,

00:01:33.058 --> 00:01:35.828
I'd get that sewn onto a pillow
and sell it in the NBC store.

00:01:35.828 --> 00:01:37.129
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.129 --> 00:01:40.099
Although the merch in
the C-SPAN store is much better.

00:01:40.099 --> 00:01:42.001
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:44.671
Now, remember,
before these hearings,

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:46.872
the only line of defense
Trump and his allies had,

00:01:46.872 --> 00:01:49.309
the line they kept repeating
over and over and over again

00:01:49.309 --> 00:01:51.444
was that there was
no quid pro quo with Ukraine.

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:53.746
-There's no quid pro quo,
no demand,

00:01:53.746 --> 00:01:55.481
no pressure, no threat.

00:01:55.481 --> 00:01:56.916
-There's no quid pro quo.

00:01:56.916 --> 00:01:58.450
-There was no quid pro quo.

00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:01.420
-There is no quid pro quo.
-There is no quid pro quo.

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:05.992
-There was no quid pro quo.
-There was no quid pro quo.

00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:08.194
-There was no quid pro quo.

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:12.732
-But listen to this.
There is no pro quo.

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:16.102
-In a way, that's Trump's
best defense.

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:17.837
"How could I be
guilty of something

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:19.772
if I can't even remember
how to say it?"

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:21.107
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.107 --> 00:02:22.108
So there you go.

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:23.543
Trump says there was
no pro quo,

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:26.312
which sounds like something a
tourist would say in Europe when

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:29.081
one of those dudes comes into
the restaurant, selling flowers.

00:02:29.081 --> 00:02:30.216
"Scuzi? No, no pro quo."

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:31.850
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.850 --> 00:02:34.286
But yesterday that talking point
was completely blown up

00:02:34.286 --> 00:02:35.955
when Trump's hand-picked
ambassador

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:37.790
to the European Union,
Gordon Sondland,

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:39.726
a businessman who donated
a million dollars

00:02:39.726 --> 00:02:42.295
to Trump's inaugural committee
and who was a central player

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:45.865
in the Ukraine scheme said there
was, in fact, a quid pro quo.

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:48.100
-Was there a quid pro quo?

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:51.103
As I testified previously

00:02:51.103 --> 00:02:53.639
with regard to the requested
White House call

00:02:53.639 --> 00:02:56.643
and the White House meeting,
the answer is yes.

00:02:56.643 --> 00:02:58.911
-Man, not only did he answer
the key question,

00:02:58.911 --> 00:03:00.279
he asked it himself.

00:03:00.279 --> 00:03:02.548
Gordon Sondland was so
determined to bring down Trump,

00:03:02.548 --> 00:03:05.118
he didn't even need anyone else
in the room with him.

00:03:05.118 --> 00:03:07.020
He could've just
interviewed himself.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:09.055
"Mr. Sondland, was there
a quid pro quo?

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:10.456
Yes, Mr. Sondland, there was.

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:12.524
And that's the T."

00:03:12.524 --> 00:03:18.363
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:18.363 --> 00:03:19.598
So there it is.

00:03:19.598 --> 00:03:21.401
He settled it definitively
once and for all --

00:03:21.401 --> 00:03:23.202
there was, in fact,
a quid pro quo.

00:03:23.202 --> 00:03:25.438
What could Trump's defense
possibly be?

00:03:25.438 --> 00:03:27.439
"I never said there was
no quid pro quo.

00:03:27.439 --> 00:03:28.441
I said there was..."

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:30.542
-No pro quo.

00:03:30.542 --> 00:03:32.612
-"Totally different."

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:34.948
So everyone in the White House
knew what was going on.

00:03:34.948 --> 00:03:36.715
In fact, Sondland
named tons of people,

00:03:36.715 --> 00:03:38.551
from Trump
to Vice President Mike Pence,

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:39.719
all the way down the chain.

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:41.887
-President Trump,
Vice President Pence,

00:03:41.887 --> 00:03:45.024
Secretary Perry,
Ambassador Volker,

00:03:45.024 --> 00:03:47.660
Secretary Pompeo,
Ambassador Bolton,

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:50.363
Chief of Staff Mulvaney,
Rudy Giuliani.

00:03:50.363 --> 00:03:52.498
-My God, it's like
he was reading from

00:03:52.498 --> 00:03:53.999
a phone book of criminals.

00:03:53.999 --> 00:03:57.170
I guess in this case, it would
be called the very white pages.

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:58.237
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.237 --> 00:04:00.105
So everyone knew
what was happening,

00:04:00.105 --> 00:04:02.574
or as Sondland put it
in his testimony yesterday...

00:04:02.574 --> 00:04:05.778
-Everyone was in the loop.

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:07.012
It was no secret.

00:04:07.012 --> 00:04:09.348
-Of course, this administration
has no secrets

00:04:09.348 --> 00:04:11.784
because every time
they do something secret,

00:04:11.784 --> 00:04:14.253
Rudy Giuliani runs to
the nearest TV camera,

00:04:14.253 --> 00:04:17.090
confesses to everything,
and gives us the evidence.

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:20.426
-Did our State Department ask
you to go on a mission for them?

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:21.694
-They did.

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:23.229
-So you did ask Ukraine
to look into Joe Biden.

00:04:23.229 --> 00:04:24.363
-Of course I did.

00:04:24.363 --> 00:04:27.166
And you know who I did it
at the request of?

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:30.837
The State Department.
It's all here, right here.

00:04:30.837 --> 00:04:33.539
-He literally confessed
to all of it

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:35.041
then showed us the evidence.

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:38.043
Rudy already held his own
impeachment inquiry by himself.

00:04:38.043 --> 00:04:41.513
He's like a guy who sees the
cops at his door and breaks down

00:04:41.513 --> 00:04:42.915
before they ask him a question.

00:04:42.915 --> 00:04:44.116
"Fine, I robbed a bank.

00:04:44.116 --> 00:04:46.018
Here's the gun I used,
and here's the cash."

00:04:46.018 --> 00:04:47.954
"Sir, I am just here
to check the meter."

00:04:47.954 --> 00:04:49.655
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.655 --> 00:04:52.024
So, in many ways,
we already knew the core facts

00:04:52.024 --> 00:04:53.292
at the heart of the case,

00:04:53.292 --> 00:04:55.795
but this week's testimony
has made it clear as day,

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:57.363
yes, there was way quid pro quo,

00:04:57.363 --> 00:04:59.298
yes, it was ordered by
the President,

00:04:59.298 --> 00:05:01.067
yes, everyone else
knew about it,

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:03.502
and, yes, it was designed
specifically to help Trump

00:05:03.502 --> 00:05:04.770
win the 2020 election,

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:07.272
which is important because
the other line of defense

00:05:07.272 --> 00:05:10.109
Republicans have used was that
Trump was concerned about

00:05:10.109 --> 00:05:11.844
corruption in Ukraine
in general.

00:05:11.844 --> 00:05:13.045
In fact, Rudy Giuliani,

00:05:13.045 --> 00:05:15.280
who is reportedly
under criminal investigation,

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:18.317
repeated that argument yesterday
in an interview with Glenn Beck,

00:05:18.317 --> 00:05:21.186
but I don't think it came out
quite the way Rudy intended it.

00:05:21.186 --> 00:05:24.957
-It's rumored they're
investigating me for bribery.

00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:28.026
I'd like to know who I bribed.

00:05:28.026 --> 00:05:29.328
I don't bribe people.

00:05:29.328 --> 00:05:32.065
I've been doing this for
50 years in my life.

00:05:32.065 --> 00:05:33.665
I've never had a complaint.

00:05:33.665 --> 00:05:35.167
I think people understand

00:05:35.167 --> 00:05:38.838
that I have a very, very great
passion for corruption.

00:05:38.838 --> 00:05:42.474
[ Laughter ]

00:05:42.474 --> 00:05:44.510
-No, that didn't --

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:47.546
that didn't come out the way
he wanted it to.

00:05:47.546 --> 00:05:49.248
You made it
sound like corruption

00:05:49.248 --> 00:05:50.416
is one of your hobbies.

00:05:50.416 --> 00:05:52.551
That's how someone would
describe themselves

00:05:52.551 --> 00:05:53.952
in their Tinder bio.

00:05:53.952 --> 00:05:56.189
"I have a great passion for
swimming, horseback riding,

00:05:56.189 --> 00:05:57.723
corruption, and pulling the skin

00:05:57.723 --> 00:05:59.425
all the way back
behind my head."

00:05:59.425 --> 00:06:02.628
You got to be careful
how you phrase stuff, man.

00:06:02.628 --> 00:06:05.330
Rudy saying he has a great
passion for corruption

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:06.765
would be like O.J. saying,

00:06:06.765 --> 00:06:09.268
"Man, I'd kill for
a ham sandwich right now."

00:06:09.268 --> 00:06:10.069
[ Laughter ]

00:06:10.069 --> 00:06:11.169
Two people?

00:06:11.169 --> 00:06:18.010
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:20.546
But obviously this was not about
corruption in general.

00:06:20.546 --> 00:06:22.547
This was about helping
Trump specifically.

00:06:22.547 --> 00:06:25.117
Yesterday, for example, Sondland
admitted in an exchange

00:06:25.117 --> 00:06:27.453
with Congressman
Sean Patrick Maloney

00:06:27.453 --> 00:06:30.256
that the investigations were
explicitly designed to benefit

00:06:30.256 --> 00:06:33.425
Trump, although it took some
coaxing to get it out of him.

00:06:33.425 --> 00:06:36.962
-Who would have benefited
from an investigation

00:06:36.962 --> 00:06:38.831
of the President's
political opponents?

00:06:38.831 --> 00:06:40.333
-I don't want to characterize

00:06:40.333 --> 00:06:42.367
who would've
and who would not have.

00:06:42.367 --> 00:06:43.969
-I know you don't want to, sir.

00:06:43.969 --> 00:06:45.037
That's my question.

00:06:45.037 --> 00:06:46.472
Would you answer it for me?

00:06:46.472 --> 00:06:47.706
-Restate your question.

00:06:47.706 --> 00:06:51.143
-Who would benefit
from an investigation

00:06:51.143 --> 00:06:53.479
of the President's
political opponent?

00:06:53.479 --> 00:06:57.650
-Well, presumably the person
who asked for the investigation.

00:06:57.650 --> 00:06:59.151
-Who is that?

00:06:59.151 --> 00:07:01.887
-If the President asked for the
investigation, it would be he.

00:07:01.887 --> 00:07:03.889
-Well, it's not a hypothetical,
is it, sir?

00:07:03.889 --> 00:07:07.593
Who would benefit from
an investigation of the Bidens?

00:07:07.593 --> 00:07:09.461
-There are two
different questions.

00:07:09.461 --> 00:07:10.830
-I'm just asking one.

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:13.199
Who would benefit from
an investigation of the Bidens?

00:07:13.199 --> 00:07:15.301
-I assume President Trump
would benefit.

00:07:15.301 --> 00:07:16.469
-There we have it, see.

00:07:16.469 --> 00:07:18.671
[ Applause ]

00:07:18.671 --> 00:07:21.106
-Trump. The answer was Trump.

00:07:21.106 --> 00:07:22.541
That exchange was excruciating.

00:07:22.541 --> 00:07:25.010
It was like watching someone
else open a pickle jar,

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:26.712
and when they
finally got it open,

00:07:26.712 --> 00:07:29.215
the only pickle inside was
one with weird hair on it.

00:07:29.215 --> 00:07:30.483
[ Laughter ]

00:07:30.483 --> 00:07:32.484
So, you heard Sondland
very clearly there.

00:07:32.484 --> 00:07:35.121
This was all orchestrated
to hurt Trump's political rivals

00:07:35.121 --> 00:07:36.455
and help the President win.

00:07:36.455 --> 00:07:38.758
And today we got more testimony
to confirm that fact

00:07:38.758 --> 00:07:41.159
from a state Department official
named David Holmes.

00:07:41.159 --> 00:07:42.894
Holmes was with Sondland
in Ukraine

00:07:42.894 --> 00:07:45.297
when Sondland called Trump to
talk about the scheme

00:07:45.297 --> 00:07:47.199
and Holmes overheard
that conversation.

00:07:47.199 --> 00:07:49.601
Now, you'll recall that
yesterday Sondland confirmed

00:07:49.601 --> 00:07:51.837
the account
that Holmes had given,

00:07:51.837 --> 00:07:53.706
an account Holmes
repeated today.

00:07:53.706 --> 00:07:56.042
-I heard Ambassador Sondland
greet the President

00:07:56.042 --> 00:07:57.943
and explain he was calling
from Kiev.

00:07:57.943 --> 00:08:00.812
I heard President Trump then
clarify that Ambassador Sondland

00:08:00.812 --> 00:08:02.147
was in Ukraine.

00:08:02.147 --> 00:08:04.116
Ambassador Sondland replied,
yes, he was in Ukraine,

00:08:04.116 --> 00:08:06.819
and went on to state
that President Zelensky

00:08:06.819 --> 00:08:09.288
"loves your ass."

00:08:09.288 --> 00:08:11.257
I then heard
President Trump ask,

00:08:11.257 --> 00:08:13.625
"So, he's going to do
the investigation?"

00:08:13.625 --> 00:08:16.094
Ambassador Sondland replied that
"he's going to do it."

00:08:16.094 --> 00:08:20.366
-He also testified that you
confirmed to President Trump

00:08:20.366 --> 00:08:23.102
that you were in Ukraine
at the time

00:08:23.102 --> 00:08:26.371
and that President Zelensky
"loves your ass."

00:08:26.371 --> 00:08:28.240
Do you recall saying that?

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:31.444
-Yeah, it sounds like
something I would say.

00:08:31.444 --> 00:08:33.946
[ Laughter ]

00:08:33.946 --> 00:08:37.582
-That is the face of a man who
has no [bleep] left to give.

00:08:37.582 --> 00:08:39.251
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:39.251 --> 00:08:40.653
"Yeah, man."

00:08:40.653 --> 00:08:44.056
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:44.056 --> 00:08:47.960
"Oh, yeah. That sounds
like Gordon Sondland.

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:50.529
About to crack open a brewski.
It's party time."

00:08:50.529 --> 00:08:51.630
[ Laughter ]

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:54.366
So Holmes overheard
Trump ask Sondland

00:08:54.366 --> 00:08:56.335
about the investigations,
and just in case

00:08:56.335 --> 00:08:59.071
it wasn't absolutely clear
what they were talking about

00:08:59.071 --> 00:09:01.307
when Sondland got off the phone
with Trump,

00:09:01.307 --> 00:09:02.675
Holmes asked him to clarify

00:09:02.675 --> 00:09:05.177
and Sondland confessed
to everything on the spot.

00:09:05.177 --> 00:09:07.313
-After the call ended,
Ambassador Sondland remarked

00:09:07.313 --> 00:09:09.181
that the President
was in a bad mood,

00:09:09.181 --> 00:09:11.516
as Ambassador Sondland stated
was often the case

00:09:11.516 --> 00:09:12.985
early in the morning.

00:09:12.985 --> 00:09:15.855
I then took the opportunity
to ask Ambassador Sondland

00:09:15.855 --> 00:09:19.225
for his candid impression of the
President's views on Ukraine.

00:09:19.225 --> 00:09:21.626
In particular, I asked
Ambassador Sondland

00:09:21.626 --> 00:09:23.895
if it was true that
the President did not give

00:09:23.895 --> 00:09:27.032
a expletive about Ukraine.

00:09:27.032 --> 00:09:29.135
Ambassador Sondland agreed
that the President

00:09:29.135 --> 00:09:31.036
did not give an expletive
about Ukraine.

00:09:31.036 --> 00:09:33.071
-Hey, man, you don't got to
bleep yourself.

00:09:33.071 --> 00:09:34.106
You could just say it.

00:09:34.106 --> 00:09:35.240
We're way past bleeping.

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:36.309
A porn star went on TV

00:09:36.309 --> 00:09:38.210
and talked about
the President's [bleep]

00:09:38.210 --> 00:09:40.045
and people dropping F-bombs
on C-SPAN.

00:09:40.045 --> 00:09:43.249
We are through
the looking glass, baby.

00:09:43.249 --> 00:09:44.450
[ Laughter ]

00:09:44.450 --> 00:09:46.785
But then Holmes continued
and said that Sondland

00:09:46.785 --> 00:09:49.087
made it clear to him
that all Trump cared about

00:09:49.087 --> 00:09:51.590
was investigating his political
rival, Joe Biden.

00:09:51.590 --> 00:09:54.126
-Ambassador Sondland agreed
that the President

00:09:54.126 --> 00:09:56.395
did not give an expletive
about Ukraine.

00:09:56.395 --> 00:09:57.596
I asked why not.

00:09:57.596 --> 00:09:59.865
Ambassador Sondland stated
that the President

00:09:59.865 --> 00:10:01.333
only cares about big stuff.

00:10:01.333 --> 00:10:04.837
I noted there was big stuff
going on in Ukraine,

00:10:04.837 --> 00:10:06.538
like a war with Russia.

00:10:06.538 --> 00:10:09.175
And Ambassador Sondland replied
that he meant big stuff

00:10:09.175 --> 00:10:10.609
that benefits the President,

00:10:10.609 --> 00:10:13.946
like the Biden investigation
that Mr. Giuliani was pushing.

00:10:13.946 --> 00:10:16.515
I briefed the call in detail to
the deputy commission,

00:10:16.515 --> 00:10:17.916
went away for a week, come back,

00:10:17.916 --> 00:10:20.085
I referred to the call,
and everyone is nodding.

00:10:20.085 --> 00:10:22.087
Of course that's
what's going on.

00:10:22.087 --> 00:10:23.188
Of course the President

00:10:23.188 --> 00:10:25.024
is pressing for
a Biden investigation

00:10:25.024 --> 00:10:27.493
before he'll do these things
the Ukrainians the want.

00:10:27.493 --> 00:10:28.994
There was nodding agreement.

00:10:28.994 --> 00:10:30.562
Everyone by that point agreed.

00:10:30.562 --> 00:10:33.265
It was obvious what
the President was pressing for.

00:10:33.265 --> 00:10:35.200
-It was obvious
this is about the Bidens.

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:36.402
Sondland said it himself.

00:10:36.402 --> 00:10:38.370
In fact, I got Rudy on FaceTime
right now.

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:40.773
Rudy, did you ask Ukraine
to investigate the Bidens?

00:10:40.773 --> 00:10:42.241
-Of course I did.
-Thank you.

00:10:42.241 --> 00:10:43.842
[ Laughter ]

00:10:43.842 --> 00:10:46.178
And if you're wondering
how Holmes could've overheard

00:10:46.178 --> 00:10:47.813
Trump speaking on
Sondland's phone,

00:10:47.813 --> 00:10:49.614
Holmes even did
a physical re-enactment

00:10:49.614 --> 00:10:51.450
to show just how loud
Trump was yelling.

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:54.386
-When the President came on,
he sort of winced

00:10:54.386 --> 00:10:58.156
and held the phone away
from his ear like this,

00:10:58.156 --> 00:11:00.692
and he did that for the first
couple of exchanges.

00:11:00.692 --> 00:11:01.927
That's how I was able
to hear it.

00:11:01.927 --> 00:11:04.163
-I definitely believe
that's how it happened.

00:11:04.163 --> 00:11:06.332
That's just how old people
talk in a phone.

00:11:06.332 --> 00:11:09.301
They think every phone is like
a ham radio during World War II.

00:11:09.301 --> 00:11:10.936
"Hello, is anyone out there?!

00:11:10.936 --> 00:11:12.404
Are you receiving this message?!

00:11:12.404 --> 00:11:14.372
Does he love my ass?!"

00:11:14.372 --> 00:11:20.412
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:11:20.412 --> 00:11:23.348
So Rudy was
at the center of this,

00:11:23.348 --> 00:11:25.884
and everything he was doing,
he did at the express direction

00:11:25.884 --> 00:11:26.685
of the President.

00:11:26.685 --> 00:11:28.053
Everyone knew what was going on,

00:11:28.053 --> 00:11:29.721
even if they weren't happy
about it.

00:11:29.721 --> 00:11:32.223
In fact, Sondland made that
clear in his testimony yesterday

00:11:32.223 --> 00:11:33.492
and again today Holmes

00:11:33.492 --> 00:11:35.327
and former national security
official Fiona Hill

00:11:35.327 --> 00:11:38.296
made it clear, using
several colorful metaphors.

00:11:38.296 --> 00:11:41.834
-President Trump directed us to
"talk with Rudy."

00:11:41.834 --> 00:11:45.771
Mr. Giuliani's requests
were a quid pro quo.

00:11:45.771 --> 00:11:48.640
Mr. Giuliani was expressing
the desires

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:50.609
of the President
of the United States.

00:11:50.609 --> 00:11:53.445
-Ambassador Bolton
had looked pained,

00:11:53.445 --> 00:11:56.448
basically indicated
with body language

00:11:56.448 --> 00:11:58.984
that there was nothing much that
we could do about it.

00:11:58.984 --> 00:12:02.188
And he then, in the course of
that discussion, said

00:12:02.188 --> 00:12:03.922
that Rudy Giuliani
was a hand grenade

00:12:03.922 --> 00:12:05.591
that was going to
blow everyone up.

00:12:05.591 --> 00:12:08.560
-Someone wondered aloud why
Mr. Giuliani was so active

00:12:08.560 --> 00:12:10.695
in the media with respect
to Ukraine.

00:12:10.695 --> 00:12:14.332
My recollection is that
Ambassador Sondland stated,

00:12:14.332 --> 00:12:15.768
"Damn it, Rudy.

00:12:15.768 --> 00:12:18.904
Every time Rudy gets involved,
he goes and effs everything up."

00:12:18.904 --> 00:12:21.106
-I love that they were all mad
at Rudy for going on TV

00:12:21.106 --> 00:12:22.374
and blabbing about their scheme.

00:12:22.374 --> 00:12:24.309
They're like guys planning
a bank heist going,

00:12:24.309 --> 00:12:25.511
"Alright, it's a perfect plan.

00:12:25.511 --> 00:12:26.812
There's no way we'll get caught.

00:12:26.812 --> 00:12:28.380
Wait, wait, wait, no, no, no,
where's Rudy?

00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:29.815
Where's Rudy?
Oh, no, no, no."

00:12:29.815 --> 00:12:31.250
[ Laughter ]

00:12:31.250 --> 00:12:32.684
So Holmes shared
his recollections

00:12:32.684 --> 00:12:34.619
of what he overheard
on the phone call with Trump.

00:12:34.619 --> 00:12:36.955
Trump was on the other end, but
he was speaking loudly enough

00:12:36.955 --> 00:12:39.257
that Holmes could hear him,
an account that Sondland himself

00:12:39.257 --> 00:12:40.425
confirmed yesterday, but still,

00:12:40.425 --> 00:12:42.061
Trump and his allies
remain unconvinced.

00:12:42.061 --> 00:12:44.296
Trump, for example, insisted
this morning that overhearing

00:12:44.296 --> 00:12:45.831
someone on a phone call
was impossible

00:12:45.831 --> 00:12:47.366
and he would know
because he's tried.

00:12:47.366 --> 00:12:50.302
-President Trump not buying it
on Twitter, explaining,

00:12:50.302 --> 00:12:51.803
"I've been watching people

00:12:51.803 --> 00:12:53.872
making phone calls
my entire life.

00:12:53.872 --> 00:12:55.908
My hearing is
and has been great.

00:12:55.908 --> 00:12:58.710
Never have I been watching
a person making a call

00:12:58.710 --> 00:13:00.379
which was not on speaker phone

00:13:00.379 --> 00:13:03.381
and been able to hear or
understand the conversation.

00:13:03.381 --> 00:13:05.684
I even tried, but to no avail."

00:13:05.684 --> 00:13:07.686
-You are a weird, weird man.

00:13:07.686 --> 00:13:08.820
[ Laughter ]

00:13:08.820 --> 00:13:11.557
What do you mean
you've been watching people

00:13:11.557 --> 00:13:13.592
make calls your entire life?

00:13:13.592 --> 00:13:15.394
What do you mean?

00:13:15.394 --> 00:13:17.629
I'm willing to bet the only
reason it didn't work is

00:13:17.629 --> 00:13:19.364
because when he listens to
phone calls,

00:13:19.364 --> 00:13:20.632
Trump stands right behind you

00:13:20.632 --> 00:13:22.300
and makes no attempt
to hide himself.

00:13:22.300 --> 00:13:24.270
"Oh, excuse me, sir.
Do you mind going away?"

00:13:24.270 --> 00:13:27.239
"No, I can't go away because I'm
listening to your phone call."

00:13:27.239 --> 00:13:28.674
Here's what we learned
this week.

00:13:28.674 --> 00:13:29.842
There was a corrupt quid pro quo

00:13:29.842 --> 00:13:31.610
in which the President
of the United States

00:13:31.610 --> 00:13:33.311
solicited a bribe
from a foreign country

00:13:33.311 --> 00:13:34.780
to interfere in
the 2020 election,

00:13:34.780 --> 00:13:35.981
and everyone knew about it.

00:13:35.981 --> 00:13:37.716
We have the testimony.
We have the evidence.

00:13:37.716 --> 00:13:39.351
That's it.
It's an open-and-shut case.

00:13:39.351 --> 00:13:40.619
The Republicans have no defense.

00:13:40.619 --> 00:13:42.688
So all they can do is lie
and attack the witnesses.

00:13:42.688 --> 00:13:44.356
I don't know what
they'll do next,

00:13:44.356 --> 00:13:46.625
but as for the Democrats, it
sure looks like they're gonna...

00:13:46.625 --> 00:13:47.826
-Impeach the [bleep]

00:13:47.826 --> 00:13:49.929
-This has been "A Closer Look."

